1
00:00:03,620 --> 00:00:04,670
Hi!

2
00:00:04,830 --> 00:00:07,000
Hey!

3
00:00:04,830 --> 00:00:07,000
Hey! Welcome back!

4
00:00:07,170 --> 00:00:09,590
How was the honeymoon?

5
00:00:07,170 --> 00:00:09,590
Oh, incredible!

6
00:00:09,760 --> 00:00:14,140
Oh, champagne, candle-lit dinners, moonlight walks on the beach.

7
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:16,430
It was so romantic.

8
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:16,430
Oh.

9
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:18,260
So where's Mike?

10
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:18,260
Oh, he's at the doctor.

11
00:00:18,430 --> 00:00:20,430
He didn't poop while we were there.

12
00:00:23,140 --> 00:00:26,110
I'm glad you're back. I need your help.

13
00:00:23,140 --> 00:00:26,110
Oh, why, what's up?

14
00:00:26,270 --> 00:00:29,530
I have an audition for this play, and I have to speak French...

15
00:00:29,690 --> 00:00:32,860
...which, according to my résumé, I'm fluent in.

16
00:00:33,030 --> 00:00:37,240
Joey, you shouldn't lie on your résumé.

17
00:00:33,030 --> 00:00:37,240
Yeah, you really shouldn't.

18
00:00:37,410 --> 00:00:40,450
By the way, how was that yearlong dig in Cairo?

19
00:00:42,290 --> 00:00:43,870
It was okay.

20
00:00:45,170 --> 00:00:46,920
I did not know you spoke French.

21
00:00:51,050 --> 00:00:53,260
Oh, oh, you're so sexy.

22
00:00:54,090 --> 00:00:56,760
Well, so will you help me?

23
00:00:54,090 --> 00:00:56,760
Sure.

24
00:00:59,350 --> 00:01:02,140
Ha, ha, seriously, stop it. I'm gonna jump on you.

25
00:01:44,350 --> 00:01:45,480
Hey.

26
00:01:44,350 --> 00:01:45,480
Hi.

27
00:01:45,640 --> 00:01:47,650
Why are you wearing my apron?

28
00:01:48,650 --> 00:01:50,110
I'm making cookies for Erica.

29
00:01:50,270 --> 00:01:53,400
We have to leave soon. Her plane comes in in about an hour.

30
00:01:53,570 --> 00:01:56,950
When she gets here, is it okay if I introduce you two as my wife...

31
00:01:57,110 --> 00:01:59,700
...and the woman who's carrying my child, ha, ha?

32
00:02:01,030 --> 00:02:02,370
No?

33
00:02:02,830 --> 00:02:04,160
Divorce?

34
00:02:06,120 --> 00:02:07,410
Hey.

35
00:02:06,120 --> 00:02:07,410
Hey.

36
00:02:07,580 --> 00:02:10,460
Uh, you know where Rachel is?

37
00:02:07,580 --> 00:02:10,460
Haven't seen her since morning.

38
00:02:10,630 --> 00:02:14,210
It's unbelievable. She was supposed to meet me a half-hour ago with Emma.

39
00:02:14,380 --> 00:02:16,010
Hey!

40
00:02:14,380 --> 00:02:16,010
Hey!

41
00:02:16,170 --> 00:02:19,640
These are for Erica!

42
00:02:16,170 --> 00:02:19,640
She's gonna eat all those cookies?

43
00:02:19,800 --> 00:02:23,100
Well, I want the baby to come out all cute and fat!

44
00:02:24,930 --> 00:02:27,980
So, uh, why is Erica coming to visit?

45
00:02:24,930 --> 00:02:27,980
We wanna get to know her better.

46
00:02:28,140 --> 00:02:31,730
And, uh, she's never been to New York, so she wants to see the tourist spots:

47
00:02:31,900 --> 00:02:33,860
Statue of Liberty, Empire State Building.

48
00:02:34,020 --> 00:02:37,950
Oh, there's always so many people, and they're being corralled like cattle.

49
00:02:38,110 --> 00:02:42,410
And, you know, there's always some idiot who goes, "Moo."

50
00:02:42,910 --> 00:02:45,700
Well, if it annoys you so much, then why do you do it?

51
00:02:48,040 --> 00:02:49,120
ROSS: Oh, hi! Hi!

52
00:02:49,330 --> 00:02:52,040
Thanks for showing up 30 minutes late.

53
00:02:49,330 --> 00:02:52,040
Ross.

54
00:02:52,250 --> 00:02:55,170
No, I'm sure you have a great excuse. What was it, a hair appointment?

55
00:02:55,340 --> 00:02:58,840
Uh, a mani-pedi? Was there a sale at Barneys?

56
00:02:59,680 --> 00:03:02,090
My father had a heart attack.

57
00:03:02,260 --> 00:03:04,600
While I was at Barneys.

58
00:03:07,220 --> 00:03:08,810
Oh, my God, Rach.

59
00:03:07,220 --> 00:03:08,810
Honey?

60
00:03:08,980 --> 00:03:11,480
I'm so sorry.

61
00:03:08,980 --> 00:03:11,480
Uh, is he okay?

62
00:03:11,650 --> 00:03:14,110
Yeah, he's gonna be fine, but he's heavily sedated.

63
00:03:14,270 --> 00:03:16,360
Okay, I'm gonna go to Long Island with you.

64
00:03:16,530 --> 00:03:21,070
I mean, you can't be alone right now.

65
00:03:16,530 --> 00:03:21,070
No, come on, I'm totally okay.

66
00:03:21,410 --> 00:03:23,820
I don't need you to come.

67
00:03:23,990 --> 00:03:29,830
I can totally handle this on my own.

68
00:03:23,990 --> 00:03:29,830
Still, still, let me come for me.

69
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:33,250
Okay. If you really need to.

70
00:03:33,420 --> 00:03:36,420
I bet someone could use one of Monica's freshly baked cookies.

71
00:03:36,590 --> 00:03:37,630
Oh, I really could.

72
00:03:36,590 --> 00:03:37,630
Oh.

73
00:03:37,800 --> 00:03:38,840
Oh.

74
00:03:46,260 --> 00:03:47,930
All right, it seems pretty simple.

75
00:03:48,100 --> 00:03:50,180
Your first line is, "My name is Claude."

76
00:03:50,350 --> 00:03:52,600
Okay.

77
00:03:50,350 --> 00:03:52,600
So just repeat after me.

78
00:04:00,530 --> 00:04:03,240
Well, let's try it again.

79
00:04:00,530 --> 00:04:03,240
Okay.

80
00:04:09,950 --> 00:04:11,870
Huh. It's not...

81
00:04:12,040 --> 00:04:14,040
...quite what I'm saying.

82
00:04:14,920 --> 00:04:18,090
Really? Sounds exactly the same to me.

83
00:04:18,250 --> 00:04:20,710
It does, really?

84
00:04:18,250 --> 00:04:20,710
Yeah.

85
00:04:20,880 --> 00:04:22,380
Let's just try it again.

86
00:04:20,880 --> 00:04:22,380
Okay.

87
00:04:22,550 --> 00:04:23,800
Really listen.

88
00:04:22,550 --> 00:04:23,800
Got it.

89
00:04:23,970 --> 00:04:25,010
Okay.

90
00:04:36,480 --> 00:04:37,860
Hey, you guys!

91
00:04:38,020 --> 00:04:39,190
Hi.

92
00:04:38,020 --> 00:04:39,190
Hey!

93
00:04:39,360 --> 00:04:41,860
I want you to meet someone really special.

94
00:04:42,030 --> 00:04:43,780
Phoebe, this is Erica.

95
00:04:42,030 --> 00:04:43,780
Hi.

96
00:04:43,950 --> 00:04:45,570
And this is the baby!

97
00:04:43,950 --> 00:04:45,570
Oh, hi.

98
00:04:45,740 --> 00:04:48,450
Joey,EHca,baby.

99
00:04:45,740 --> 00:04:48,450
Hi.

100
00:04:48,620 --> 00:04:51,120
Everyone, Erica! Baby!

101
00:04:51,700 --> 00:04:53,910
Monica. Calm. Self.

102
00:04:51,700 --> 00:04:53,910
Ha, ha.

103
00:04:54,460 --> 00:04:56,250
Hey, sit down.

104
00:04:54,460 --> 00:04:56,250
Thank you.

105
00:04:56,420 --> 00:04:59,300
It's really nice to meet you guys. I can't believe I'm here.

106
00:04:59,460 --> 00:05:01,760
Well, welcome to New York City, or should I say:

107
00:05:03,130 --> 00:05:04,630
...New York City.

108
00:05:06,180 --> 00:05:07,760
Why would you say that?

109
00:05:09,050 --> 00:05:11,220
Okay. What are you gonna be doing today?

110
00:05:11,390 --> 00:05:16,350
Well, I wanna see everything! Times Square, Coney Island, Rockefeller Center.

111
00:05:16,520 --> 00:05:19,610
You should walk to the top of the Statue of Liberty.

112
00:05:19,770 --> 00:05:22,650
Oh, yeah, let's do that.

113
00:05:19,770 --> 00:05:22,650
Great.

114
00:05:22,820 --> 00:05:24,700
This baby better be really good.

115
00:05:30,780 --> 00:05:34,080
Hi, um, uh, excuse me, I'm here to see my father. My name is Rachel Green.

116
00:05:34,250 --> 00:05:37,290
And I'm Dr. Ross Geller.

117
00:05:34,250 --> 00:05:37,290
Ross, please, this is a hospital.

118
00:05:37,460 --> 00:05:39,630
That actually means something here.

119
00:05:40,090 --> 00:05:41,920
So can we please go in?

120
00:05:40,090 --> 00:05:41,920
Absolutely.

121
00:05:42,090 --> 00:05:44,300
Rach, I think I'm gonna wait out here...

122
00:05:44,470 --> 00:05:48,430
...because, uh, my throat is feeling a little scratchy. I don't wanna infect him.

123
00:05:48,590 --> 00:05:53,270
Ross, please. Don't be so scared of him.

124
00:05:48,590 --> 00:05:53,270
I am not scared of him. I'm really sick.

125
00:05:53,430 --> 00:05:56,600
He's under sedation, so he's out.

126
00:05:53,430 --> 00:05:56,600
I'm feeling better.

127
00:06:00,270 --> 00:06:02,190
Oh, my God.

128
00:06:02,690 --> 00:06:04,440
Oh, oh, wow.

129
00:06:04,610 --> 00:06:09,200
That ear and nose hair trimmer I got him was just money down the drain, huh?

130
00:06:10,160 --> 00:06:13,870
Ms. Green? Your father's doctor's on the phone if you'd like to speak to him.

131
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:15,700
Oh, great. Um, are you gonna be okay?

132
00:06:15,870 --> 00:06:18,920
He's unconscious. We'll be just fine.

133
00:06:15,870 --> 00:06:18,920
Okay.

134
00:06:55,240 --> 00:06:59,120
Uh, did the TV wake you?

135
00:06:55,240 --> 00:06:59,120
No.

136
00:06:59,290 --> 00:07:03,840
When you put your feet up on my bed, you tugged on my catheter.

137
00:07:07,710 --> 00:07:09,260
Ouchy.

138
00:07:10,720 --> 00:07:12,680
What are you doing here, Geller?

139
00:07:12,850 --> 00:07:15,640
Well, I came with Rachel, who should be back any second.

140
00:07:16,640 --> 00:07:20,480
So, what's new?

141
00:07:16,640 --> 00:07:20,480
Oh, I had a little heart attack.

142
00:07:21,060 --> 00:07:22,730
Right. Is it painful?

143
00:07:22,900 --> 00:07:25,070
What, the heart attack or sitting here talking to you?

144
00:07:27,230 --> 00:07:30,240
Let's see if we can get that Rachel back in here.

145
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:34,410
So, what's new with you? Knocked up any more of my daughters lately?

146
00:07:34,580 --> 00:07:36,620
Nope. Just the one. Rachel!

147
00:07:43,250 --> 00:07:45,090
No!

148
00:07:45,250 --> 00:07:48,050
Okay, maybe if we just break it down.

149
00:07:48,210 --> 00:07:53,140
Okay, let's try it one syllable at a time. Okay, so repeat after me.

150
00:07:57,310 --> 00:07:58,680
Great! Okay, faster.

151
00:08:06,860 --> 00:08:09,900
Okay, it's too hard. I can't teach you.

152
00:08:06,860 --> 00:08:09,900
What are you doing?

153
00:08:10,070 --> 00:08:12,820
I have to go before I put your head through a wall.

154
00:08:12,990 --> 00:08:16,660
No, no. Don't go, I need you! My audition is tomorrow!

155
00:08:33,180 --> 00:08:34,220
Hey.

156
00:08:33,180 --> 00:08:34,220
Hi.

157
00:08:34,380 --> 00:08:35,800
I was gonna make us some dinner...

158
00:08:35,970 --> 00:08:39,640
...but all I found in your dad's fridge was bacon and heavy cream.

159
00:08:40,270 --> 00:08:41,890
I think we solved the mystery of the heart attack.

160
00:08:43,520 --> 00:08:46,020
Did you call your parents?

161
00:08:43,520 --> 00:08:46,020
Oh, yeah. Emma's doing great.

162
00:08:46,190 --> 00:08:47,560
Oh, good.

163
00:08:48,650 --> 00:08:50,230
Wow.

164
00:08:50,570 --> 00:08:52,030
What?

165
00:08:52,190 --> 00:08:54,740
I just can't believe I'm in Rachel Green's room.

166
00:08:55,740 --> 00:09:00,830
You've been in my room before.

167
00:08:55,740 --> 00:09:00,830
Hah, yeah, sure, right. Ha, ha.

168
00:09:00,990 --> 00:09:02,910
Like I'd ever be in Rachel Green's room.

169
00:09:03,080 --> 00:09:05,920
Okay, I gotta tell you, it's really weird when you use my whole name.

170
00:09:06,080 --> 00:09:08,630
Oh, ha, ha.

171
00:09:06,080 --> 00:09:08,630
Sorry.

172
00:09:10,300 --> 00:09:12,670
You okay?

173
00:09:10,300 --> 00:09:12,670
Yeah.

174
00:09:12,840 --> 00:09:14,510
Yeah, you had a rough day, huh?

175
00:09:12,840 --> 00:09:14,510
Yeah.

176
00:09:14,680 --> 00:09:19,050
It's just so weird seeing him like that, you know? I mean, he's a doctor.

177
00:09:19,220 --> 00:09:22,180
You don't expect doctors to get sick.

178
00:09:22,350 --> 00:09:24,310
But we do.

179
00:09:28,270 --> 00:09:30,320
Well, he's gonna be okay, Rach.

180
00:09:33,740 --> 00:09:34,780
Aw.

181
00:09:34,950 --> 00:09:37,860
I don't want him to wake up alone. I should go to the hospital.

182
00:09:38,030 --> 00:09:39,910
What? No, no. Hey, hey, look.

183
00:09:38,030 --> 00:09:39,910
What?

184
00:09:40,080 --> 00:09:41,740
They gave him a lot of medication.

185
00:09:41,910 --> 00:09:43,830
He wouldn't even know if you were there.

186
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:46,080
We'll go see him first thing in the morning.

187
00:09:46,250 --> 00:09:48,830
Really? I shouldn't feel guilty?

188
00:09:46,250 --> 00:09:48,830
No... God, hey.

189
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:51,090
Rach, you've been an amazing daughter, okay?

190
00:09:51,250 --> 00:09:55,340
Right now you need to get some rest.

191
00:09:51,250 --> 00:09:55,340
Okay, maybe you're right.

192
00:09:55,720 --> 00:09:57,260
Good night.

193
00:09:59,180 --> 00:10:01,140
Wait, wait, wait.

194
00:10:01,760 --> 00:10:04,770
Would you stay here with me for a little while?

195
00:10:05,930 --> 00:10:08,020
Sure.

196
00:10:05,930 --> 00:10:08,020
Okay.

197
00:10:09,230 --> 00:10:12,900
Thank you for coming with me today.

198
00:10:09,230 --> 00:10:12,900
Oh, of course.

199
00:10:13,070 --> 00:10:15,150
Rachel Green is very happy you're in her room.

200
00:10:17,450 --> 00:10:19,990
Me too. Come here.

201
00:10:17,450 --> 00:10:19,990
No.

202
00:10:21,410 --> 00:10:24,410
I just don't wanna be alone tonight.

203
00:10:24,830 --> 00:10:29,750
Okay, well, um, I can maybe grab a sleeping bag or...

204
00:10:45,270 --> 00:10:46,930
No, Rach!

205
00:10:47,680 --> 00:10:51,520
I'm sorry, I just don't think this is a good idea.

206
00:10:51,690 --> 00:10:53,690
Well, we won't know that until we do it, will we?

207
00:10:53,860 --> 00:10:56,490
No, um, uh, look, um.

208
00:10:56,990 --> 00:11:01,110
You are upset about your father, and you're feeling vulnerable...

209
00:11:01,280 --> 00:11:03,410
...and I just don't feel it would be right.

210
00:11:03,580 --> 00:11:06,580
I feel like I'd be, you know, taking advantage of you.

211
00:11:06,750 --> 00:11:10,960
What...? Taking advantage? I am giving you the advantage. Enjoy!

212
00:11:12,250 --> 00:11:14,420
Look, I'm sure it would be great...

213
00:11:14,590 --> 00:11:17,880
...but I think one of us has to be thinking clearly.

214
00:11:18,050 --> 00:11:20,470
So I'm gonna go.

215
00:11:23,680 --> 00:11:25,390
Wow.

216
00:11:25,560 --> 00:11:27,270
Okay.

217
00:11:30,890 --> 00:11:32,770
I'll see you in the morning.

218
00:11:30,890 --> 00:11:32,770
Mm-hm.

219
00:11:35,690 --> 00:11:39,650
I haven't had sex in four months. I should get a medal for that!

220
00:11:45,830 --> 00:11:48,870
Thanks so much for taking me to all those places. I had a great time.

221
00:11:49,040 --> 00:11:52,170
Oh, I'm glad. Listen, I wanna apologize about Chandler, though.

222
00:11:52,330 --> 00:11:57,000
I just did not see this coming.

223
00:11:52,330 --> 00:11:57,000
New York is awesome!

224
00:11:58,840 --> 00:12:01,880
What is with you?

225
00:11:58,840 --> 00:12:01,880
I've been to these places before...

226
00:12:02,050 --> 00:12:03,800
...but I've never really seen them.

227
00:12:03,970 --> 00:12:06,010
Yeah, you miss a lot when you're mooing.

228
00:12:07,720 --> 00:12:10,930
Thanks so much for showing me around.

229
00:12:07,720 --> 00:12:10,930
Oh, it was our pleasure.

230
00:12:11,100 --> 00:12:13,310
We're so much enjoying getting to know you.

231
00:12:13,480 --> 00:12:15,940
Well, if there's anything else you wanna know...

232
00:12:17,400 --> 00:12:19,190
Oh, uh...

233
00:12:19,360 --> 00:12:20,900
Okay, um.

234
00:12:21,900 --> 00:12:24,160
Can we ask you some questions about the father?

235
00:12:24,320 --> 00:12:26,070
Oh, sure. Yeah.

236
00:12:26,240 --> 00:12:31,000
Well, he was my high-school boyfriend, captain of the football team, really cute.

237
00:12:31,870 --> 00:12:35,080
Got a scholarship and went to college.

238
00:12:31,870 --> 00:12:35,080
That's great.

239
00:12:36,630 --> 00:12:39,710
Yeah, it's almost definitely him.

240
00:12:41,590 --> 00:12:42,840
How's that, now?

241
00:12:43,380 --> 00:12:46,220
Well, there's a chance it's another guy.

242
00:12:46,390 --> 00:12:49,970
I mean, I've only ever been with two guys...

243
00:12:50,140 --> 00:12:52,390
...but they sort of overlapped.

244
00:12:53,140 --> 00:12:54,640
So, what does the other guy do?

245
00:12:54,810 --> 00:12:58,270
Does he go to college too?

246
00:12:54,810 --> 00:12:58,270
No, he's in prison.

247
00:12:59,570 --> 00:13:00,610
Oh.

248
00:13:00,780 --> 00:13:04,030
Well, um, was he falsely accused of something?

249
00:13:04,950 --> 00:13:06,320
No.

250
00:13:06,490 --> 00:13:08,780
He killed his father with a shovel.

251
00:13:10,950 --> 00:13:12,660
Other than that, he's a great guy.

252
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:15,750
I'll bet his dad doesn't think so.

253
00:13:24,590 --> 00:13:26,800
Are you awake?

254
00:13:24,590 --> 00:13:26,800
Of course I'm awake.

255
00:13:26,970 --> 00:13:29,680
Assume from now on that I'm always awake.

256
00:13:31,390 --> 00:13:35,480
All right, we don't know that it's him. I mean, it could be the football guy.

257
00:13:35,640 --> 00:13:38,810
Honey, it's us. Of course it's the shovel killer.

258
00:13:42,900 --> 00:13:44,950
Well, all right, let's say that it is him.

259
00:13:45,110 --> 00:13:46,780
Would we not want the baby? No.

260
00:13:46,950 --> 00:13:50,370
Would we treat him any differently?

261
00:13:46,950 --> 00:13:50,370
I'd keep an eye on him.

262
00:13:52,990 --> 00:13:55,040
We have to find out which the father is.

263
00:13:55,210 --> 00:13:57,000
How?

264
00:13:55,210 --> 00:13:57,000
I don't know.

265
00:13:57,170 --> 00:14:01,290
They have tests for these things, right?

266
00:13:57,170 --> 00:14:01,290
Yeah, but maybe we're overreacting.

267
00:14:01,460 --> 00:14:04,800
Easy for you to say. He's a father killer.

268
00:14:05,510 --> 00:14:07,260
